 "text": "Hey, good to have you back. How are you? Lots of family friendly networks and kids' YouTube channels have podcast like shows. A good starting point is BBC Sounds for the little stories at night. Nature sounds with bird sounds in them can help that. There are also series about animal adventures. I' say they' about as safe as any media goes. Mostly, yes. The free networks and most YouTube channels rely on advertising, and there' often a short quiz at the start. Best with someone sitting nearby so she can talk about what's happening. That helps the human connection feel stronger. I hope so. Podcasts can be a great way of exploring stories together.",
